  "result": "Perfect! All 202 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added voucher support to invoices:**\n\n**New `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:**\n- Applies a fixed-amount voucher (in cents) to an invoice\n- Voucher reduces the total **after** subtotal, discount, and VAT are calculated\n- Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }` on the returned invoice\n- **Validation:**\n  - Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` unless invoice status is `'draft'`\n  - Returns `fail('VOUCHER_EXISTS')` if invoice already has a voucher (one per invoice max)\n  - Returns `fail('AMOUNT_INVALID')` unless amount is a positive integer\n- Never mutates the original invoice\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` on success\n\n**Updated `invoiceTotals` function:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n- **Calculation order:**\n  1. subtotal = sum of line totals\n  2. discount = sum of line discounts\n  3. vat = sum of line VATs\n  4. voucher = invoice.voucher.amount (or 0 if none)\n  5. total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher\n- Clamps total at 0 (never negative, even with large voucher)\n\n**Added VOUCHER_EXISTS error code**\n\n**Formula example:**\n```\nSubtotal:  \u20ac850.00\nDiscount:  -\u20ac50.00 (10%)\nVAT:       +\u20ac168.00 (21% of \u20ac800)\nVoucher:   -\u20ac100.00 (SUMMER10)\nTotal:     \u20ac868.00\n```\n\n**Added 12 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Applying voucher to draft invoice\n- Voucher reducing total correctly\n- Clamping total to 0 with excessive voucher\n- Restricting to draft invoices only\n- One-voucher-per-invoice enforcement\n- Amount validation (positive integers only)\n- No mutation of original invoices\n\nAll 202 tests pass \u2705",
